# Normalise line endings on the way into the repository.
#
# Without this, every commit from Windows tripped the `mixed-line-ending`
# pre-commit hook, which rewrote the files and failed, so each commit had to be
# made twice. The hook was right and the fix belongs here: git decides what is
# stored, the working tree keeps whatever the platform wants.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Not text. `text=auto` guesses well and a wrong guess corrupts these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
